{"step_index":519,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:32Z","thinking":"**Defining Customer Order Endpoint**\n\nAdding a new route handler within the sales module. This route will manage direct purchases or online orders placed by customers from verified pharmacies. It will be a POST endpoint with the `/customer-order` path.\n\n\n**Validating Customer Order Details**\n\nVerifying that both `pharmacyId` and `medicineId` are present in the request body, rejecting the order if either is missing. The quantity defaults to 1 if not specified or invalid.\n\nRetrieving pharmacy and medicine details using provided IDs. Checking stock availability in the pharmacy's inventory.\nIf no specific batch is provided, a search for any available stock item in the inventory for the specified medicine and pharmacy is performed. If there is no stock, the request will be rejected.\n\nChecking if sufficient quantity is available to fulfill the order. Constructing appropriate responses based on inventory status.\n\n\n**Calculating Order Costs and Handling Users**\n\nCalculating the total price using the medicine's selling or reference price, then generating a unique receipt identifier. Retrieving or creating a user record based on the provided customer information.\n\nUpdating the pharmacy inventory by reducing the stock based on the order quantity, then updating the item. Constructing a sale record including medicine details, customer information, and financial details.\n\n**Recording the Sale and Medicine History**\n\nIf a linked user exists, then creates an entry in medicine history indicating a purchase. The entry includes customer details, medicine information, batch details, and the transaction type, along with pharmacy information.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\server\\\\routes\\\\history.js\"","EndLine":"76","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"View history.js complete\"","toolSummary":"\"View server/routes/history.js\""}}]}
{"step_index":520,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:40Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T02:22:40+06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T02:22:40+06:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/User/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/medcheck-bd/server/routes/history.js`\nTotal Lines: 76\nTotal Bytes: 2102\nShowing lines 1 to 76\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: const express = require('express');\n2: const router = express.Router();\n3: const MedicineHistory = require('../models/MedicineHistory');\n4: const { protect } = require('../middleware/auth');\n5: const { authorizeRoles } = require('../middleware/roles');\n6: \n7: // @route   GET /api/history\n8: // @desc    Get current customer's verification and purchase history\n9: // @access  Private/Customer\n10: router.get('/', protect, authorizeRoles('customer', 'admin'), async (req, res) => {\n11:   try {\n12:     const { type } = req.query;\n13:     const query = { customerId: req.user._id };\n14: \n15:     if (type && type !== 'ALL') {\n16:       query.type = type;\n17:     }\n18: \n19:     const history = await MedicineHistory.find(query)\n20:       .populate('medicineId')\n21:       .populate('pharmacyId', 'name address phone area')\n22:       .sort({ checkedAt: -1 });\n23: \n24:     res.json({\n25:       success: true,\n26:       count: history.length,\n27:       data: history,\n28:     });\n29:   } catch (err) {\n30:     res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: err.message });\n31:   }\n32: });\n33: \n34: // @route   DELETE /api/history/:id\n35: // @desc    Delete a specific history item\n36: // @access  Private/Customer\n37: router.delete('/:id', protect, authorizeRoles('customer', 'admin'), async (req, res) => {\n38:   try {\n39:     const item = await MedicineHistory.findOne({\n40:       _id: req.params.id,\n41:       customerId: req.user._id,\n42:     });\n43: \n44:     if (!item) {\n45:       return res.status(404).json({ success: false, message: 'History record not found' });\n46:     }\n47: \n48:     await item.deleteOne();\n49: \n50:     res.json({\n51:       success: true,\n52:       message: 'Record removed from history',\n53:     });\n54:   } catch (err) {\n55:     res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: err.message });\n56:   }\n57: });\n58: \n59: // @route   DELETE /api/history\n60: // @desc    Clear all history for customer\n61: // @access  Private/Customer\n62: router.delete('/', protect, authorizeRoles('customer'), async (req, res) => {\n63:   try {\n64:     await MedicineHistory.deleteMany({ customerId: req.user._id });\n65: \n66:     res.json({\n67:       success: true,\n68:       message: 'Medicine history cleared successfully',\n69:     });\n70:   } catch (err) {\n71:     res.status(500).json({ success: false, message: err.message });\n72:   }\n73: });\n74: \n75: module.exports = router;\n76: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":521,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:40Z","thinking":"**Adding Medicine Intake Logging**\n\nExamining the route definition, the plan involves creating a `POST` endpoint at `/api/history`. This endpoint will enable users, specifically customers and administrators, to manually log medicine intake details to their history. The route will be secured with authentication and authorization.\n\n\n**Enhancing history endpoint integration**\n\nThe `GET /api/history` endpoint needs to incorporate sales data for a complete customer purchase history. The approach involves checking the `Sale` collection for customer purchases not already present in `MedicineHistory`. The existing sort order can be retained by using `req.user._id` to query `MedicineHistory`. Additional `Sale` records can be identified using `sale.customerPhone`.\n\nAnalyzing the front-end, medicine purchases seem to be recorded in `pharmacy-details.html`. The table structure suggests that an action column will be added to enable tracking.\n\n\n**Implementing Direct Purchase Options**\n\nThe goal is to provide a consistent \"Buy\" action across multiple views: `pharmacy-details.html`, `verify.html`, and `price.html`.  Adding \"Buy\" buttons to these views will utilize the same customer order modal. A reusable modal will be developed to handle order submissions from each context.\n\nThe `View Stock & Prices` button in `pharmacies.html` will be updated to direct users to `pharmacy-details.html`, streamlining the purchasing process by allowing a 1-click buy option from pharmacy details. The modal, housed in `client/js/main.js`, will need to accept medicine, pharmacy, and batch details as input to render dynamically.\n\n\n**Addressing history loading failures**\n\nThe initial hypothesis is that immediate redirection prevents viewing local history when not logged in. Implementing a guest mode banner on `history.html`, instead of redirection, allows users to view local data. A prominent \"Login as Demo Customer\" button will be added in this guest mode.\n\nLogged-in users would fetch history via a secured API call.  If the response status indicates an authentication error, investigate authentication header usage in the request.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\client\\\\js\\\\main.js\"","EndLine":"484","StartLine":"450","toolAction":"\"View end of main.js\"","toolSummary":"\"View end of main.js\""}}]}
