{"step_index":523,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:50Z","thinking":"**Designing the Customer Order Modal**\n\nConsidering the `openCustomerOrderModal` function and its expected input `opts` to design the customer order modal. The modal's purpose is to display order details, so it needs to clearly present medicine information, pharmacy details, and other relevant order data. The `opts` object structure guides this design, as it provides all required details to be displayed.\n\n\n**Determining Modal Trigger Location**\n\nThe \"Buy/Order\" button's placement is in `pharmacy-details.html`, dynamically generated within the stock table. This is handled by `loadPharmacyDetails()` that renders `stockTableBody` using `stock.map()`. The modal will be triggered when a user clicks the order button on the pharmacy details page.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\client\\\\history.html\"","EndLine":"173","StartLine":"70","toolAction":"\"View history.html script\"","toolSummary":"\"View history.html script\""}}]}
